Krita Nova 53 - finger-friendly menus (Android)

Menu items were too close together to hit the right one with a finger, and a
tap was too short to see which one was hit.

- KisTouchFriendlyStyle::sizeFromContents(): menu items (not separators) are
  at least MENU_ITEM_HEIGHT (40) high - every menu: the menu bar's, the
  Layers docker's "+" menu, context menus, ...
- MenuTapFeedback (an application event filter): when a finger (or mouse)
  is released over a menu item, the item is highlighted and the release is
  held back for MENU_TAP_FEEDBACK_MS (150 ms), then replayed - the menu acts
  and closes after the tapped line was shown. Separators, disabled items and
  submenus behave as before.

Android only (KisTouchFriendlyStyle is only used there).
